      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AMAROO STAR (2) dipped at the end of last campaign but he was in super form prior to that. His trial coming into this was very good and the claim of Cooper comes in handy. Should land in a beautiful position and if he can return somewhere near his best, he'll be hard to fend off. LONG SERVICE LEAF (6) boasts a brilliant record over this course and distance, though he was disappointing here last week when an odds-on favourite. Was off a freshen there, so he may be better now with the cobwebs blown off. Expecting a much better run this time around. GIRLS DAY OUT (7) comes back to 1000m now after a good win fresh. Brad Parnham reunites now having a good record aboard the mare and her early speed is a highlight. Can give a bold sight. SWINGMAN (4) can resume on a positive note with some strong formlines from his last campaign. LORD SHIVA (3) won't be far away on his recent form.",
